DeskWall is an independent project inspired by Deskland Preview
(https://github.com/BLEZZ0102/Deskland, GPL-3.0, Copyright (C) 2026 Deskland authors).
The original Deskland source was imported as this repository's first commit and is kept in
git history. The current DeskWall code (Rust/Tauri host, settings app and all themes, built on
DeskWall's own classic/kit.js) is a new implementation; the themes that followed Deskland's
scenes most closely ("Beach", "Meadow" and "Isles") were removed on 2026-11-20. The
desktop-attachment approach in apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/desktop/windows.rs follows the
technique documented in Deskland's host, and the "Thaw" theme's icon field and grass hatching
still follow the approach of Deskland's prototype pages. DeskWall is not affiliated with or
endorsed by the Deskland authors, and does not use the Deskland name, logo or icon as its own.

The "Thaw" theme (apps/desktop/public/themes/classic/thaw.*) is DeskWall's own work in the same
format. Its plant and stone sprites (assets/thaw-sprites.webp) are rendered with
tools/thaw/render_sprites.py from Quaternius' "Stylized Nature MegaKit" (CC0,
https://quaternius.com); its ground tiles
(assets/thaw-snow/earth/green/grass.webp) are derived from Poly Haven's snow_02, mud_forest,
brown_mud_leaves_01 and grass_ground (CC0, https://polyhaven.com). Birds and snowflakes are painted at startup.

Third-party dependencies keep their own licenses (see each package's metadata).
